From e39d68a9837c46552f6a5aa082e582d3abe5fd27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venkatakrishnaiah Pari <vpari@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:19:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: core: Skip sync_state when pd_ignore_unused is set

When booted with the pd_ignore_unused kernel command line parameter,
generic PM domains are intentionally left powered on and are not
torn down by genpd_power_off(). Calling of_genpd_sync_state() in this
mode still walks the gpd_list and attempts to power off each domain
tied to the provider, which is pointless work and contradicts the
intent of pd_ignore_unused.

Bail out of of_genpd_sync_state() early when pd_ignore_unused is set.

Signed-off-by: Venkatakrishnaiah Pari <vpari@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/core.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
index 52ea84e548ff..85bd5bffe345 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
@@ -3506,6 +3506,9 @@ void of_genpd_sync_state(struct device_node *np)
 	if (!np)
 		return;
 
+	if (pd_ignore_unused)
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&gpd_list_lock);
 	list_for_each_entry(genpd, &gpd_list, gpd_list_node) {
 		if (genpd->provider == of_fwnode_handle(np)) {
-- 
2.34.1

